\f1\fs22 Sarah slept, close to coma, until the dawn light met her\'97grim, defeated and wide-eyed. Tony\'92s snoring frightened the morning sun under a fluffy blanket of the Layer.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>On the surface, Sarah was terrified by the Gyges Disc and the pursuit of deranged PAPER agents. She\'92d never before felt so incapable of running the engine of her own destiny. Dark agents had amassed and were syphoning the petrol from her tank.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Under her surface terrors lurked deeper unease. In the clarity of the morning, Sarah recalled a second dream, one in which she was visited by a tall and sinister vampire with an epic fantasy beard, wearing Elvi garb. The most unsettling aspect of the dream was that, rather than sucking blood from her, Sarah could not shake the dull sense the vampire had injected something inside her.
